Commanding plunger motion. Watch the plunger, not the screen.
Bounded to +3 mm of forward travel, then asked for it back.
This firmware moves at ~0.673 s/mm; ~0.1 s means it did not.

  -- HOME --
  HOME (cold)              dt=  26.35s  reply=ERR:{"error":"Failed to home pipette"}       pos=0.0 homed=0
  -- forward: does distance scale? --
  MOVE_TO 1.0 mm           dt=   0.67s  reply=OK:{"msg":"Pipette moved","v":[1.00]}        pos=1.0 homed=0
  MOVE_TO 3.0 mm           dt=   1.33s  reply=OK:{"msg":"Pipette moved","v":[3.00]}        pos=3.0 homed=0
  -- HOME from a non-zero position: does it retract? --
  HOME (from 3.0)          dt=  26.35s  reply=ERR:{"error":"Failed to home pipette"}       pos=3.0 homed=0
  -- backward: the same positions, asked for in reverse --
  MOVE_TO 3.0 mm           dt=   0.01s  reply=OK:{"msg":"Pipette moved","v":[3.00]}        pos=3.0 homed=0
  MOVE_TO 1.0 mm (back)    dt=   1.33s  reply=OK:{"msg":"Pipette moved","v":[1.00]}        pos=1.0 homed=0
  MOVE_TO 0.0 mm (back)    dt=   0.67s  reply=OK:{"msg":"Pipette moved"}                   pos=0.0 homed=0

VERDICT: the plunger moves in both directions. If it still
  does not dispense, the problem is the mm/uL calibration or
  the mechanical coupling to the plunger.
